usage: franklinwh-cli [-h] [--version] [--config PATH] [--email EMAIL] [--password PASS] [--gateway SN] [--installer] [--json]
                      [--no-color] [-v] [--trace MODULES] [--api-trace] [--log-file PATH]
                      {status,st,discover,disc,mode,tou,energy,raw,metrics,monitor,mon,accessories,acc,sc,smart-circuits,gen,generator,network,net,diag,diagnostic,bms,battery,support,snapshot,schema,fetch} ...

Command-line interface for the FranklinWH Cloud API.

positional arguments:
  {status,st,discover,disc,mode,tou,energy,raw,metrics,monitor,mon,accessories,acc,sc,smart-circuits,gen,generator,network,net,diag,diagnostic,bms,battery,support,snapshot,schema,fetch}
                        Command to execute
    status (st)         Live system overview (power, SOC, mode, weather, metrics)
    discover (disc)     Gateway, device, warranty, and accessory enumeration
    mode                Get or set operating mode
    tou                 Time-of-Use schedule inspection and control
    energy              Energy (kWh) and 5-minute power (kW) history — table, JSON or CSV
    raw                 Direct API method passthrough
    metrics             Show API call metrics from current session
    monitor (mon)       Real-time battery dashboard (auto-refresh, Ctrl+C to exit)
    accessories (acc)   Accessory inventory, status, and device info (Smart Circuits, V2L, Generator)
    sc (smart-circuits)
                        Detailed Smart Circuit configuration and control
    gen (generator)     Generator module configuration and live metrics
    network (net)       Inspect the aGate's connection, or put it back on WiFi
    diag (diagnostic)   Diagnostic report — system, auth, device, power, API health
    bms (battery)       Battery Management System — cell telemetry, pack health, bus topology
    support (snapshot)  System snapshot for troubleshooting — export, redact, compare
    schema              Show Current/Totals field schema — Python attr → raw API key mapping
    fetch               Arbitrary GET/POST to any API endpoint

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit

credentials:
  --config, -c PATH     Path to franklinwh.ini config file
  --email, -e EMAIL     FranklinWH account email
  --password, -p PASS   FranklinWH account password
  --gateway, -g SN      aGate serial number
  --installer           Use installer account login (LOGIN_TYPE_INSTALLER). Default: homeowner account

output:
  --json, -j            Output as JSON
  --no-color            Disable ANSI colour output

debug:
  -v, --verbose         Increase verbosity (-v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace)
  --trace MODULES       Enable debug for specific modules (comma-sep: stats,modes,tou,storm,power,devices,account,client,all)
  --api-trace           Show per-call API trace with timing
  --log-file PATH       Write debug output to file
